        "original_id": "4e005b7e-7c20-5962-b2b6-1dc3e3e2fe20",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Bands: Wire, Young the Giant, Moonshake, Laika\n- People: Colin Newman, Graham Lewis, Bruce Gilbert, Robert Gotobed, Margaret Fiedler McGinnis, PJ Harvey\n- Songs: \"Cough Syrup\"\n- Places: London, Irvine, California\n\nFacts:\n- Wire is an English rock band that was formed in London in October 1976 by Colin Newman, Graham Lewis, Bruce Gilbert, and Robert Gotobed.\n- Colin Newman was a vocalist and guitarist in Wire when the band formed.\n- Graham Lewis was a bassist and vocalist in Wire when the band formed.\n- Bruce Gilbert was a guitarist in Wire when the band formed.\n- Robert Gotobed was a drummer in Wire when the band formed.\n- Young the Giant is an American rock band that formed in Irvine, California, in 2004.\n- Margaret Fiedler McGinnis is best known as a founding member of the UK indie groups Moonshake and Laika.\n- Margaret Fiedler McGinnis also performed as a live guitarist with PJ Harvey and Wire.\n- \"Cough Syrup\" is a song by Young the Giant from the band's self-titled debut album.",
